Diagonal and off-diagonal first_token_changed rates are indistinguishable (0.079 vs 0.062). Ablating one class's direction is no more disruptive to its own class's prompts than to other classes' prompts. The Stage 3.1 behavioural effect is real but not class-specific at layer 3 — the directions point at a shared 'noetic-shaped' axis, not at distinct per-class features. This bounds the mechanistic claim sharply.

